  "label": "Stereotype linking Islam to terrorism",
  "description": "This is a common and harmful stereotype that falsely associates Islam with terrorism. It is used to justify discrimination, violence, or political repression against Muslims. The meme uses this stereotype implicitly by pairing the phrase 'piece of you over here, piece of you over there' with a Muslim man, suggesting that even a peaceful-looking Muslim is somehow connected to violence or chaos, which is a core tenet of Islamophobic rhetoric.",
